WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.150
Professor Charles Xavier.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.170
Mutant leader.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.880
Loving caretaker.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.880
Genius teacher.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.040
And total, absolute jerk.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.540
And it's not just that he does some pretty
messed up stuff sometimes.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.900
Occasionally, Professor X goes full-on supervillain.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:24.010
For all of Xavier's talk about peace and love
and harmony, he's the most unscrupulous, hypocritical,

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.269
and manipulative of all the X-Men.

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.929
Face it: Magneto was right.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:35.770
Professor X is downright dangerous, and nothing—not
even death—can stop him.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.329
Easy A

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:42.820
You'd think that a man who runs a school would
have some respect for the education system...

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.379
but you'd be wrong.

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:49.879
When Professor X was just regular old Charles
Xavier, he totally scammed his way through

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:51.910
high school in the worst way.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.480
He wasn't even subtle.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.940
In class, Charles would read his teachers'
minds for answers, and he became the star

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.140
quarterback by psychically stealing plays
from the opposing team.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.450
And did he show any remorse about abusing
his powers?

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:11.270
At home, Charles devoted an entire shelf to
the trophies he didn't really earn, so…

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.270
no.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.610
He only retired from athletic competition
because he got bored of how severely he dominated

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.120
all of the puny humans.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.440
Kinda makes you feel not even too bad about
the whole leg thing.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.220
When Charles' half-brother Cain Marko saw
through the charade, he went mad with jealousy,

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.380
forcing Chuck to put him down with a karate
chop.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.710
Later, Charles tried to convince his students
that Cain was the true villain, but here's

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:42.360
all you need to know: after Charles' stepfather
died, he kept the family's fortunes to himself,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.180
while Cain transformed into Juggernaut and
worked as a hired gun.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:51.420
We're not saying that Charles is the bad guy
here, but after all of the X-Men are bedridden

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.330
because of Juggernaut's personal vendetta
against Charles that they had nothing to do

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.330
with… he makes them sweep up the mansion.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.600
Certified jerk move.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.600
Student body

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.750
When Jean Grey showed up at old man Xavier's
School for Gifted Youngsters, she was noticed

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.170
by pretty much everyone…

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.760
except Iceman, who had his own reasons that
weren't revealed for about fifty years.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:19.970
Angel, Beast, and-- Cyclops all instantly
have the hots for Jean, and when Wolverine

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.340
shows up, it's more of the same.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:28.940
There's also the creepy bald mentor who serves
as both Jean's teacher and her surrogate father

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:35.430
figure... and lusts after Jean in secret for
years, after slapping her in a skin-tight

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.430
costume.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:42.230
Thankfully, aside from a single panel in X-Men
#3 in which Professor X laments that the only

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:48.960
thing keeping him and Jean apart is his disability,
yeah right, the issue only comes up once more,

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.650
but in a very big way.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:57.180
In the '90s, When Professor X's darkest thoughts
manifested themselves as an alternate personality

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:02.440
called Onslaught, his crush on Jean makes
a surprising re-appearance, making it clear

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.010
that Xavier's had a thing for Jean for years.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:10.370
It's unsettling at best, and makes a lot of
those early X-Men comics, in which Jean is

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:15.040
clearly the Professor's favorite student,
a whole heck of a lot creepier.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.090
Control yourself, dude.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.090
Big fake out

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:23.730
Professor X used some pretty interesting methods
to train the unruly mutants at his school,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:28.470
and when throwing them into the life-threatening
Danger Room wasn't enough, he wasn't above

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.120
using psychological abuse to keep them in
order.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.120
"Thanks, Jubilee!”

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.260
“You were right!”

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.530
“Xavier’s totally rad!”

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:42.770
In X-Men #4, Xavier "loses" his powers, only
to reveal an issue later that—surprise!—he

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.420
was faking in order to give the X-Men a pop
quiz.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.400
In X-Men #42, it gets even worse.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.860
In a battle with a creature called Grotesk
the Sub-Human, an explosion takes Xavier's

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.360
life, and the X-Men spend the next two years
mourning.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.360
Two years.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:04.569
And yet, in X-Men #65, Xavier smugly rolls
back into their lives, alive and perfectly

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:05.569
healthy.

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:08.490
Because the guy who died wasn't even Xavier
in the first place.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.900
As it turns out , he'd swapped places with
a shape-shifting mutant called Changeling,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.160
who was basically the world's most dangerous
Make-A-Wish kid.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.870
Changeling, a former villain, had been diagnosed
with a terminal illness and wanted to use

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:27.080
his last few months on Earth to make a difference,
so Professor X let him lead the X-Men.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:33.440
Meanwhile, Xavier locked himself in a basement
and devised a plan to defeat an impending

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.300
alien invasion.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.470
When Changeling fell during battle, Professor
X decided to let them grieve instead of letting

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.650
them in on the gag.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.630
For two years.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.620
Class act, Charles.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.120
Giant-Size Jerk

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.710
In Giant-Size X-Men #1, Professor X recruits
a brand new group of X-Men—including mainstays

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:58.940
like Wolverine, Nightcrawler, Storm, and Colossus—to
rescue his original band of mutants from Krakoa

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.950
the Living Island, rebooting the struggling
X-Men series in the process.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:09.030
However, as the X-Men learn in Deadly Genesis,
in a storyline basically lifted from Futurama,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.900
complete with a bald old weirdo genius, our
heroes are actually the B-squad.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:19.010
"Are you three by any chance interested in
becoming my new spaceship crew?”

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.010
“NEW crew?

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.100
What happened to the old crew?”

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.080
“Oh, those poor sons of… that's not important!”

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:28.300
Before Cyclops led the new group of X-Men
to victory, Xavier deployed an entirely different

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.680
group of superheroes to rescue his former
students—and then erased everyone's memory

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.090
of the team when they all apparently died.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.730
Unfortunately for Xavier, one of those mutants
actually survived and called him out: Gabriel,

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:46.860
a mutant with the code-name Vulcan, who also
happened to be the little brother of Cyclops

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.010
and Havok.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:53.110
After the mission to Krakoa goes south, Cyclops
is understandably distraught by Vulcan's supposed

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:58.460
death, so Xavier deletes all of Scott's memories
of his brother in order to keep him calm.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.990
That doesn't work out so well when Vulcan
returns from space.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:06.620
In his quest for vengeance, Vulcan kills a
few mutants, and tells Cyclops and Havok the

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.460
truth, turning them against Xavier.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:14.880
Together, the X-Men stop Vulcan, but Cyclops
banishes a now-powerless Xavier from the X-Mansion.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.610
Because honestly, erasing your team leader's
memory of his awesome space-bro because you

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:22.639
got him killed is a tool move.

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:24.570
The Xavier Protocols

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:28.630
Everyone knows that when Batman created a
series of plans to kill his Justice League

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.770
teammates, it didn't work out so well.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:36.050
Everyone knows, except for Professor X...
who did the exact same thing.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.949
Yes, the surrogate father and mentor of the
X-Men figured out, in detail, how to kill

00:06:40.949 --> 00:06:44.800
each one of them, which is revealed in Excalibur
#100.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.680
After Onslaught takes over Professor X's mind,
the X-Men visit Moira MacTaggert's research

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:55.199
lab to retrieve the Xavier Protocols, which
explain how to murder every mutant on the

00:06:55.199 --> 00:06:56.199
team.

00:06:56.199 --> 00:06:57.199
Need to get rid of Wolverine?

00:06:57.199 --> 00:06:59.639
Simply sever his head and put it somewhere
else.

00:06:59.639 --> 00:07:00.970
Got a problem with Cable?

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.229
Just amp up the techno-virus that's slowly
consuming his body, allowing the disease to

00:07:05.229 --> 00:07:07.140
ravage his brain and body.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:11.440
A suit of anti-psionic armor will topple Professor
X himself.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.780
If you guessed that this story doesn't have
a happy ending, well, you know how comics

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:17.780
work.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:24.259
In X-Men #65, a human-Sentinel hybrid named
Bastion uses the Xavier Protocols to defeat

00:07:24.259 --> 00:07:25.259
the team.

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:30.900
In X-Men #84, Professor X's mutant-tracking
computer Cerebro comes to life and uses the

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.540
Protocols against the X-Men when they try
to stop it from taking over humanity.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:41.820
In both cases, the X-Men prevail, but not
for Professor X's lack of trying.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:42.820
Brain drain

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:48.550
After Cyclops killed Professor X at the end
of Avengers vs. X-Men, most people assumed

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.400
Xavier's reign of terror was over.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.560
They were wrong.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:57.210
In Uncanny Avengers #1, the Red Skull steals
Professor X's brain and uses its psychic powers

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.460
to try and wipe out mutantkind for good.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.080
It almost works, too.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.840
Using Xavier's powers, the Red Skull brainwashes
the Scarlet Witch, who drove mutants to the

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.120
brink of extinction in House of M, and tries
to get her to do it again.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:17.030
Next, he incites an anti-mutant mob in Manhattan,
and manipulates Thor into turning against

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.030
his teammates.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:23.840
Later, the Red Skull transforms himself into
Red Onslaught and uses Professor X's powers

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:29.520
to start "World War Hate"—and when the Avengers
and the X-Men try to use a spell to bring

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:35.169
out Xavier's better nature, they inadvertently
turn all of the heroes into villains and all

00:08:35.169 --> 00:08:40.240
the villains into heroes, kicking off Marvel's
epic AXIS event.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.440
That's Chuck for you.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.560
Dead for years, and still up to no good.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:44.560
Thanks for watching!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.389
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:47.389 --> 00:08:50.059
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

